CHY3 is organized around a single journey: find and validate an idea, build a monetization path, then improve the economics with data. Each stage has a dedicated module; all of them share one API layer and one event system.

# Incubate

IdeaForge handles the cold start. An AI-assisted ideation engine turns a sentence into a structured outline and feasibility read. A prototype generator produces an interactive web or mobile mockup. A community review system puts the premise in front of real people before the team commits months to it.

# Validate

ValueFlow aggregates transactions from every payment provider in use, then shows which content, channel, and cohort produced the revenue. Funnels, attribution, and forecasting turn a vague sense of “what works” into a model that can be inspected and challenged.

# Scale

CreaSDK packages payments, subscriptions, distribution, and community operations as standard modules. A team can adopt one primitive or the whole stack. The design goal is to compress months of monetization plumbing into weeks.

# Coordinate

The Creator Marketplace, launching in Q4 2026, is the layer where the three stages meet: ideas incubated in IdeaForge, business models validated in ValueFlow, and capabilities delivered through CreaSDK.
